Man pages: a plain \- between the name and the description in NAME.

The NAME lines of mwm(1), uil(1), xmbind(1), mwmrc(4), Traits(5), UIL(5)
and WML(5) separate the name and the description with \(em. The whatis
line that man -k and the man front-end read is taken from "name \- text",
the -man convention, so these pages had none. Only the NAME line changes;
the rest of each page, and the section-3 pages, are as upstream wrote them.

--- a/doc/man/man1/mwm.1	2026-11-19 13:42:24.264247049 +0200
+++ b/doc/man/man1/mwm.1	2026-11-19 13:42:24.350598576 +0200
@@ -48,7 +48,7 @@
 .ta 8n 16n 24n 32n 40n 48n 56n 64n 72n 
 .TH "mwm" "user cmd"
 .SH "NAME"
-\fBmwm\fP \(em The Motif
+\fBmwm\fP \- The Motif
 Window Manager
 .SH "SYNOPSIS"
 .PP
